Stage 3: the campaign MISSION-SELECT screen (f338 "INTRODUCTORY CAMPAIGN") + the ec7e-OK dispatch tail
+ the FUN_0000_f0f1 .CAM mission-record parser.

Clicking OK in the SELECT A CAMPAIGN screen (ec7e) now runs its tail: f0f1 parses the selected campaign's
.CAM into the mission-record table, e78c writes the player .FPL (6ade) and opens FUN_0000_f338 = the
"INTRODUCTORY CAMPAIGN" modal screen -- a left column of mission rows (state-coloured marker box + the
map-thumbnail background baked into the screen .MRL), the selected mission's name + two briefing lines at
the bottom, and ACCEPT/CANCEL.  Its first settled frame is bit-identical (AE=0) to a genuine DOSBox capture
on native + wasm.  The deeper ACCEPT->7088 screen / mission start is a separate deliverable.

All asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (+ re_out/fist_mga_image.bin for the box primitives).

THE .CAM MISSION PARSER (FUN_0000_f0f1 + handlers, asm 0xf0f1..0xf334).  f0f1 reopens the selected
campaign's .CAM (filename letter [0xf889]='A'+campaign) via bd14 (open + op-0x80 decrypt, patch 147), then
walks its keyword tokens: f05f copies a token to DGROUP:0xf902, f088 matches it against the 19 STRSEG
keyword strings (b91b[]) returning a byte-index bx, and the handler at word[DGROUP:0xf822+bx] fills the
mission-record table (records at DGROUP:0x6dda, stride 0xfd, count [0x6dd0]).  Ghidra base-lost the whole
family -- the handler dispatch `*(word*)(bx-0x7de)` (bx used as a host pointer), every `[0xf89b]+off`
record write (record base used as a host pointer), the STRSEG base of efd8/f00c, and folded all the carry
flags to a static false so the loop never terminated / dispatched garbage.  Reconstructed faithfully:
 - efd8 (skip-to-digit) / f00c (atoi): rebase source to STRSEG (word[DGROUP:0x70]<<4), set CF via g_fist_cf.
 - f0f1: dispatch = word[DGROUP:0xf822+bx]; loop CF via g_fist_cf.
 - the record handlers f146/f154/f1a1/f1ec/f24a/f282/f299/f2c0/f2e7/f30e: rebase every record field write
   to g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)([0xf89b]+off); CF via g_fist_cf.  (f0cc already rebases its DGROUP-offset arg,
   patch 147, so the pure-copy handlers f1da/f202/f214/f226/f238/f25d/f26f were already correct.)

THE f338 SCREEN (asm 0xf338 + FUN_1000_bd7e/bdbe/be47/bea4, the cdc4-lesson method set).
 - FUN_0000_f338: the modal loop, reconstructed like ec7e/cc33 (patch 137/148) -- Ghidra folded the carry
   to a static in_CF so it never terminated.  Template 0x2d37 at DGROUP:0xfa77; dispatch flag ba56
   (0=idle,1=ACCEPT,0xff=CANCEL); bd7e runs at entry.
 - FUN_1000_bd7e (mission availability): rebase the record base (0x6dda); the required-count read (rec+0x31)
   is a WORD.
 - FUN_1000_bdbe (bottom selected box): thread the dropped [0x60a] fill (rect 0xfa80, colour 0); rebase the
   record base (Ghidra used `unaff_CS`) to 0x6dda + [0x6db6]*[0xfa88]; draw name (rec+0) + the two 0x3e-byte
   briefing lines (rec+0x7c, rec+0xbc) with the 0xf8->0x17 colour fixup.
 - FUN_1000_be47 (per-mission marker boxes): reconstruct the dropped al(state colour)/bx(rect rec+0x19)
   args for the [0x61e]/[0x61a]/[0x622] box primitives (sig (rect,colour), same family as 119f/11db); the
   selected mission blinks on [0x452]&0x10; colour by availability rec+0x3b (0->0x21/2->0x20/else 0x22).
 - FUN_1000_bea4 (hover hit-test): rebase the record base for the rect test.

